.TH SHOPNO-UPDATE-HELPER 1 "November 2026" "shopno-update-helper 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shopno-update-helper \- check for and install system and Flatpak updates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shopno-update-helper
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shopno-update-helper
refreshes the package lists, shows what
.B apt-get full-upgrade
would change, and lists Flatpak apps and runtimes with updates.
On request it installs the system packages first, then the Flatpak updates.
.PP
System packages are installed in a terminal inside the window, so questions
asked by packages, such as debconf dialogs and configuration file prompts,
can be answered there. The terminal opens by itself when a package asks
something, and can be opened at any time with
.BR Details .
.PP
Refreshing the package lists and updating Flatpak apps need no password for
the active local user. Installing system packages asks for an administrator
password once, through polkit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/shopno-update-helper/apt-refresh
Runs
.B apt-get update
as root. Started through
.BR pkexec (1).
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/shopno-update-helper/apt-upgrade
Runs
.BR "dpkg \-\-configure \-a" ,
.B apt-get \-f install
and
.B apt-get full-upgrade
as root. Started through
.BR pkexec (1).
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/com.jadupc.shopno-update-helper.policy
Who may run the helpers.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B G_MESSAGES_DEBUG=shopno-update
Print debug messages.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt-get (8),
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR polkit (8)
